^CONVERSION ERROR$
^(ERROR|error): operand of unary
--
N5008 [dcl.init.aggr]/1, [dcl.init.list]/3: a class with a user-declared
converting constructor is not an aggregate, so It{ref_member} calls the
constructor; the reference-member argument must be dereferenced exactly once.
CBMC previously mis-classified the converting constructor as a copy constructor
(attempting aggregate init) and double-dereferenced the reference member
(*(*this->root)).  This is the expr_iterator.h layer of the rename_symbol.cpp
cascade.  assertion.2 FAILURE proves non-vacuity.
